{
  "rationale": "This is iteration 0, so there is no race telemetry or integration feedback yet. I am setting a balanced baseline and will use the first race to test the main geometry questions. Sensors: five 12 mm sensors spread across x = -0.04 to +0.04 (8 mm spacing, covering about 0.09 m). That gives enough sideways span to read the 25 mm tape at moderate offsets, and the outer sensors can still see the line on sharp bends. They sit at y = 0.05 m, ahead of the axle, so the controller gets look-ahead and can respond before the wheels reach the curve. Drivetrain: wheel_track 0.12 m and wheel_radius 0.03 m, a middle setting that gives agile turning without too much slip, and a comfortable speed margin for the 1.5 m/s average needed to finish in 3 s. Mass 0.7 kg keeps yaw inertia low for fast steering changes while leaving enough traction. Body width 0.12 m: the off-track limit is max(0.06, 0.0125 + 0.03) = 0.06 m, so body width is effectively irrelevant at this value. Body length 0.16 m is a neutral choice with no direct dynamic effect. Expected result: completion on the development tracks with a modest number of line-loss events. The main uncertainty is whether a 0.09 m sensor span is too wide for tight slalom bends or too narrow for fast sweeps, which the race data should show.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.7
  },
  "intent": "Baseline symmetric five-sensor array with forward look-ahead at y = 0.05 m and a medium-agility drivetrain. Purpose: establish a clean reference for how sensor span and forward offset affect line tracking, before I change any single factor.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "questions": [
      "Does the Integrator's controller saturate or oscillate with this sensor span (0.09 m) on the slalom and s-bend tracks?",
      "Is 0.12 m wheel track giving enough turn authority, or does the robot understeer at the sharpest bends?",
      "Does the forward offset of 0.05 m give useful lead, or does it cause lag and overshoot?",
      "Is the mass of 0.7 kg causing any speed or traction limits at base speeds near 2?"
    ],
    "measurements": ["completion", "progress", "completion_time", "rms_error", "max_error", "line_loss_events", "steering_oscillation", "controller_errors"]
  },
  "learning": "Iteration 0 has no evidence, so the hypotheses are untested. Expected: sensor span is the main driver of tracking error and oscillation; forward offset mainly affects overshoot on bends; wheel track and mass mainly affect turn rate and speed limits. Next step: compare rms_error and steering_oscillation against sensor span and look-ahead once race data arrives."
,
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor array",
      "notes": "Symmetric five-sensor baseline with 0.09 m span, forward look-ahead at 0.05 m, 0.12 m track, 0.7 kg. No prior evidence exists yet, so this sets a reference for the first race to test span and look-ahead."
    }
  }
}
